  "text": "מיתי\nLet's solve the problem step by step.\n\nFirst, we know that the sum of the lengths of any two consecutive sides of the polygon is equal to the length of the opposite side. So, we can write:\n\n$$A_1A_2 + A_2A_3 + A_3A_4 + \\ldots + A_{10}A_{11} + A_{11}A_1 = 20$$\n\nSince the sum of the lengths of any two consecutive sides is equal to the length of the opposite side, we have:\n\n$$A_1A_2 = A_2A_3 = A_3A_4 = \\ldots = A_{10}A_{11} = A_{11}A_1$$\n\nLet's denote the length of each consecutive side as $a$. Then we can write:\n\n$$11a = 20$$\n\nSolving for $a$, we get:\n\n$$a = \\frac{20}{11}$$\n\nNow, we need to find the area of the polygon. We can use the formula for the area of a polygon with equal consecutive sides and equal opposite angles:\n\n$$\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{4} \\times (a^2 + a^2 + \\ldots + a^2 + a^2) \\times \\sin(\\theta)$$\n\nwhere $\\theta$ is the angle between two consecutive sides.\n\nWe know that $\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{12}{13}$, so we can find $\\sin(\\theta)$ using the identity $\\sin^2(\\theta) + \\cos^2(\\theta) = 1$:\n\n$$\\sin^2(\\theta) = 1 - \\cos^2(\\theta) = 1 - \\left(\\frac{12}{13}\\right)^2 = \\frac{169}{169} - \\frac{144}{169} = \\frac{25}{169}$$\n\nTaking the square root, we get:\n\n$$\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{5}{13}$$\n\nNow, we can find the area of the polygon:\n\n$$\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{4} \\times (11a)^2 \\times \\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 121a^2 \\times \\frac{5}{13}$$\n\nSubstituting $a = \\frac{20}{11}$, we get:\n\n$$\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 121 \\times \\left(\\frac{20}{11}\\right)^2 \\times \\frac{5}{13} = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 121 \\times \\frac{400}{121} \\times \\frac{5}{13} = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 400 \\times \\frac{5}{13} = \\frac{500}{13}$$\n\nNow, we need to express $A_1A_2 + A_1A_{11}$ as a fraction in the form $\\frac{m\\sqrt{n} - p}{q}$. We know that $A_1A_2 = A_{11}A_1 = a = \\frac{20}{11}$, so:\n\n$$A_1A_2 + A_1A_{11} = 2a = 2 \\times \\frac{20}{11} = \\frac{40}{11}$$\n\nWe can write $\\frac{40}{11}$ as $\\frac{40\\sqrt{1} - 0}{11}$, so $m = 40$, $n = 1$, $p = 0$, and $q = 11$. Therefore, $m + n + p + q = 40 + 1 + 0 + 11 = \\boxed{52}$.",
